    63	## 8. Critique of the Codex consult
    64	codex-consult-v2.md did not exist when this plan was written; no critique.
     1	The best next step is **one X-sign calculation using global ideal membership, followed by a full Rees-fiber certificate**. The supplied X-plus and X-minus inputs are related by an exact sign substitution, so their expensive computations can be shared. Iso needs a completion argument beyond its quadratic relations. The Azure failures already distinguish artificial address-space exhaustion from genuine memory pressure.
     2	
     3	The commands below are proposed runs. I performed read-only inspection and exact coefficient comparisons; I launched no acquisition, cloud job, package build, or long algebra computation.
     4	
     5	**First fix the mathematical target**
     6	
     7	Write
     8	\[
     9	A=(k[t]/J)_{\mathfrak m},\qquad I=(G_1,\ldots,G_s)A,\qquad
    10	F(I)=\bigoplus_{d\ge0}I^d/\mathfrak m I^d.
    11	\]
    12	The requested algebraic object is \(\operatorname{Proj}F(I)\), with its embedding, dimension, degree, Hilbert series, and preferably components. A finite initial Hilbert-function segment supplies partial information. The brief explicitly requires that distinction. [purpose.md:23–29](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/purpose.md:23)
    13	
    14	Two qualifications matter:
    15	
    16	- **The supplied \(G\) represents kernel-map coordinates.** The producer constructs principal four-Pfaffians of a rank-four Schur form for nullity-eight sources. Consequently, the relevant blow-up center is the coordinate ideal \(I=(G)\). Identifying \(I\) with the ideal of the boundary orbit \(Z\), as the purpose note does, needs a separate equality proof. Replacing \(I\) by \(I(Z)\) or \(\mathfrak m\) generally changes the exceptional fiber. [nullity16_basepoints.py:283–294](~/worktrees/IBMQuantum/a5-kernel-attachments/docs/evidence/a5-kernel-attachments/nullity16_basepoints.py:283), [purpose.md:12–20](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/purpose.md:12)
    17	- **A completed calculation over \(\mathbb F_{32009}\) certifies that reduction.** The original producer distinguishes modular calculations from calculations over \(\mathbb Q(i)\). Agreement at several primes supports reconstruction; complex component claims require characteristic-zero verification or a suitable specialization argument. [nullity16_rees_fibers.py:119–123](~/worktrees/IBMQuantum/a5-kernel-attachments/docs/evidence/a5-kernel-attachments/nullity16_rees_fibers.py:119), [nullity16_rees_fibers.py:634–650](~/worktrees/IBMQuantum/a5-kernel-attachments/docs/evidence/a5-kernel-attachments/nullity16_rees_fibers.py:634)
    18	
    19	**What the retained failures establish**
    20	
    21	The product and module counts below follow directly from the displayed generator lists and loops.
    22	
    23	| Run | Actual computation | Cost boundary and retained result |
    24	|---|---|---|
