    67	## msolve
    68	
    69	Authority: `msolve -h` of the binary in use. The passagemath wheel 10.8.13
    70	ships msolve 0.10.1 linked to libgomp, FLINT and GMP; the build host's
    71	system package is 0.11.0, so a measured row names its binary and holds only
    72	for that version.
    73	
    74	| Flag | Meaning | Setting for Rees eliminations |
    75	|---|---|---|
    76	| `-f FILE`, `-o FILE` | input, output | required |
    77	| `-e N` | two-block DRL elimination order, first N variables eliminated | number of eliminated variables (`-e 1` for the variable `a`) |
    78	| `-g 0/1/2` | print nothing / leading ideal / full reduced basis for the first prime | `-g 2` when the basis is the result |
    79	| `-t N` | OpenMP threads | physical cores free for the job (2 on a Standard_FX4mds_v2 alone, 1 beside another job); hyperthreads add contention |
    80	| `-s N` | initial hash table size 2^N (default 17) | `-s 24` skips early doublings |
    81	| `-u N` | rebuild the hash table every N steps, dropping stale monomials (default 0, never) | `-u 2` when the monomial table drives memory |
    82	| `-m N` | maximum pairs per matrix (default unlimited) | leave unlimited: it splits matrices without shrinking the monomial table |
    83	| `-l 1/2/42/44` | exact sparse-dense / exact sparse (default) / probabilistic variants | `-l 2`; the probabilistic modes stay out of cited results |
    84	| `-r 0/1` | reduce the final basis (default 1) | default |
    85	| `-q 0/1` | signature-based F4 | experiment only |
    86	| `-v 0/1/2` | verbosity; 2 prints per-step degree and matrix sizes | `-v 2`, the only progress trace |
    87	| `-c`, `-d` | genericity handling for zero-dimensional solving | irrelevant to elimination |
    88	
    89	There is no `-l 0`, no column-split option, and `-s` takes an exponent, not a
    90	count.
    91	
    92	Environment: `OMP_PLACES=cores OMP_PROC_BIND=close MALLOC_ARENA_MAX=2`.
    93	
    94	Build: the wheel's F4 library (`libneogb`) carries no AVX-512 code and almost no
    95	AVX2; its AVX2 and AVX-512 routines serve FGLM only. A Standard_FX4mds_v2
    96	(Xeon Platinum 8573C) offers AVX-512 F/VL/BW/IFMA/VNNI. A native build
    97	(`-O3 -march=native` on the target host) vectorizes the row reductions; the
    98	expected speedup per step is unmeasured, and memory does not change.
    99	
   100	Accuracy: computations over a prime field with `-l 1` or `-l 2` are exact and
   101	deterministic.
   102	
   103	Version pin. The build host runs the distribution package and each Azure VM a
   104	native build of the same upstream release, so both sit on upstream's latest
   105	tag. Read the tag with
   106	`gh api repos/algebraic-solving/msolve/releases/latest -q .tag_name` and the
   107	host's version with `msolve -V`; when they differ, update the host package and
   108	rebuild on each VM:
   109	
   110	```sh
   111	sudo apt-get install -y build-essential autoconf automake libtool pkg-config libgmp-dev libmpfr-dev libflint-dev git
   112	git clone --depth 1 --branch "$TAG" https://github.com/algebraic-solving/msolve.git "msolve-src-$TAG"
   113	cd "msolve-src-$TAG" && ./autogen.sh
   114	CFLAGS="-O3 -march=native -mtune=native -fopenmp -funroll-loops" ./configure --prefix="$HOME/msolve-$TAG"
   115	nice -n 19 make -j2 && make install
   116	"$HOME/msolve-$TAG/bin/msolve" -V
   117	objdump -d "$HOME/msolve-$TAG/lib/libneogb.so" | grep -c zmm   # nonzero: AVX-512 kernels present
   118	```
   119	
   120	A launch line names the binary by its versioned prefix, never the wheel's
   121	`sage_wheels/bin/msolve`. The v0.11.0 native build on a Standard_FX4mds_v2
   122	carries 199 AVX-512 instructions in `libneogb`; the passagemath wheel carries
   123	none.
   124	
   125	## Singular 4.4
   126	
   127	Singular's `std`, `slimgb`, `syz`, `eliminate` and `minAssGTZ` run on one
   128	thread. `Singular --help` lists `--cpus`, `--threads` and `--flint-threads`;
   129	they bound the parallel libraries (`parallel.lib`, `tasks.lib`) and FLINT or NTL
   130	calls, not a single standard-basis computation. Parallelism for these
   131	eliminations comes from separate processes through `parallel.py` or separate
   132	hosts.
   133	
   134	| Setting | Meaning |
   135	|---|---|
   136	| `option(redSB)` | reduced standard bases; set before the first `std` |
   137	| `option(prot)` | prints progress only; no memory effect |
   138	| `option(notWarnSB)` | silences warnings on non-standard-basis inputs |
   139	| ordering | global (`dp`, `lp`, block orders) per the repository canon; local orderings (`ds`) run far slower on the A_5 strata |
   140	| `GOROROBA_WORKERS` | worker count for the repository's process pools |
   141	
   142	Cap: cgroup `MemoryMax` or the RSS watchdog. Singular's allocator reserves
   143	little beyond its resident set, so an address-space cap usually works, but the
   144	cgroup cap is the uniform rule.
