    12	of each of the seven boundary orbits. One moved point uses a rational unipotent `G_2(C)` automorphism whose 60
    13	candidate nilpotent derivations span the 14-dimensional derivation algebra; the other uses the rational boost with
    14	`c=5/4` and `s=3/4`. All 21 points retain the expected closure-membership pattern and real left nullity.
    15	
    16	Write the bordered skew matrix as
    17	
    18	`A(z, conjugate(z)) = A^(1,0)(z) + A^(0,1)(conjugate(z))`.
    19	
    20	The antiholomorphic part occupies only the scalar border. At every tested point, an exact principal-Pfaffian frame
    21	`F` of the boundary kernel has zero scalar-coordinate row. The producer also multiplies the matrices directly and
