    46	The exact [`partner_purity.py`](partner_purity.py) replay reconstructs `C_z` directly from the repository
    47	Cayley-Dickson signs and matches the interior block of the bordered-matrix implementation. It verifies symbolically
    48	that `C_z` is skew and `C_z z=0`; hence `z^T C_z=0`. If the complex kernel vector `(a,u)` represents a partner, its
    49	lower kernel equation is
    50	
    51	`a conjugate(z) + C_z u = 0`.
    52	
    53	Multiplication by `z^T` gives `a z^T conjugate(z)=0`. On the real A_5 locus, the second factor is the sum of the 30
    54	squares of the real and imaginary coordinates of `z`, so the factor is positive for a nonzero left element.
    55	**Inferred:** `a=0`, and inversion of the split-complex coordinate map gives zero `e_0` and `e_16` coordinates for
    56	every partner. The antiholomorphic derivative occupies only the scalar border, so its restriction to every such
    57	kernel vanishes. The item-1 complex-linearity conclusion therefore holds at every nonzero doubly pure boundary point,
