    31	## 2. Where the gaps are
    32	
    33	- **N1. Generic compact-orbit dimensions and moduli** on the unit sections of W8 (real dimension 23), E8-bar (21), Iso
    34	  (21) and X_+- (19). Their dimensions at the recorded representatives versus at generic points are unknown. Expect
    35	  larger moduli than at nullity 12.
    36	- **N2. Stabilizer types and their strata** inside each nullity-8 orbit: which stabilizers occur, where they jump, and
    37	  how the jump loci sit relative to the closure order.
    38	- **N3. Fiber representations** of each stabilizer on the complex rank-4 kernel, and their restrictions at the
    39	  boundary of each moduli space. A boundary orbit of nullity 12 must contain the nullity-8 representation plus two
    40	  extra dimensions; the shape of that specialization is the attaching data for item 6.
    41	- **N4. Unit-section topology** of each nullity-8 orbit, as far as the invariants need it.
    42	- **N5. Transition data, structure group and classes** of each nullity-8 kernel bundle. A rank-4 complex bundle over a
    43	  base of real dimension 19 to 23 lies outside the stable range of cancellation for most pieces, so triviality needs
