     1	# Iso->N+ degree-3 fiber cone: what stalled and what to run instead
     2	
     3	Tags: [F] read from file (path:line), [I] inferred, [M] measured by me in a probe (Singular 4.4 system binary, p=32009, same G and J, 8 GiB cap, 10 min cap).
     4	
     5	## 1. What input.sing computes
     6	- [F] input.sing:1 ring `32009,(t2..t7),ds` (local, origin). :2 J, one quadric. :3 G, 17 generators (the loop bound 17 at :5).
     7	- [F] :5 Pr = all 969 = C(19,3) cubic products G[i]G[j]G[l]. :6 U = Pr, J, t_k*Pr (k=2..7): 969+1+6*969 = 6784 = "RESULT U_size 6784" (result.json). :7 S = syz(U). :8-10 C = constant terms of S on the 969 Pr slots; h3 = 969 - rank(C).
     8	- [I] Let I = G*A, A = R_m/(J). Then rank(C) is the dimension of {c : sum c_b Pr_b in (J) + m*I^3}, the degree-3 part of the defining ideal of the fiber cone F(I) = sum_d I^d/mI^d (the Rees special fiber). h3 = dim F_3 = number of local minimal generators of I^3. "Degree-3 fiber relations" = rank(C) cubic relations among G1..G17.
     9	- [I] Global equals local here: I^3/(mI^3) is killed by m, so (P+J)/(mP+J) is the same module before and after localizing; syz generators evaluated at 0 give the same L over polynomial cofactors.
    10	
    11	## 2. Why it stalls
    12	- [F] singular.log: degree markers 2, 18, 19, 20, 21, 22 with 6783, 6782, 6906, 6591, 4859, 2202 pairs. Pair count peaked at 6964 (pair #125), then fell almost linearly; the last printed count is 1820 at 41,052 s. [I] The premise "pair count rising" holds only for the first ~125 steps; the run was in degree 22, still falling, not diverged. ETA unknown (new pairs keep spawning); 12 h cut it off.
    13	- Local ordering: [F] input.sing:1 `ds`; order of G is 2 (t4*t5-type tails), so cubes sit at order 6 to 18+ and Mora normal forms carry ecart growth. [M] d=2 same script: 54 s, 0.5 GB (1072 gens); d=3 has 6.3x the gens.
    14	- Module size: [F] 6784 columns, Schreyer-style syz tracks all components; samples.tsv: RSS 11.3 GB at 80 s, 17.3 GB at 39,000 s. Memory was not the killer; single thread time was.
    15	- Redundant generators: [I] 969 cubics span far less than 969 mod relations; [M] below, only 265 can be independent.
    16	- Coefficient field: not a cause. [F] p=32009, i=10754 split prime (input.sing:3), per memory note singular-split-prime-not-extension.
    17	
    18	## 3. Measured facts to anchor every option
    19	- [M] h1 = 17 (rank_C 0; syz in 0 s): G is a minimal generating set, so no generator can be dropped.
    20	- [M] h2 = 85, rank_C(2) = 68, local `syz` of (Pr, J, t_k*Pr), 54 s, 0.5 GB.
    21	- [M] The 68 quadric relations generate in k[T1..T17] a Hilbert function 17, 85, 265, 640 (degrees 1-4). So rank_C(3) >= 969-265 = 704 and h3 <= 265.
    22	- [M] Global dp `syz(Pr,J)` at d=2 did not finish in 400 s (exit 124), against 54 s for the ds route: the global-ordering doctrine (AGENTS.md "Computer algebra") does not transfer to this module syzygy; it concerns local invariants of ideals, not syzygy-module size.
    23	- [M] `minbase` (local ring, ideal Pr,J) at d=2: 86 generators, h2 = 85, 20 s, 0.3 GB, equal to the syz route.
    24	- [M] d=3 `minbase` on full 969 and on the 265-monomial reduction: neither finished in 560 s (RSS 3.7 and 5.2 GB). Cost class is hours, not minutes.
    25	
    26	## 4. Ranked alternatives
    27	1. **Quadric-reduced cubic basis (cuts 969 to 265, exact).** [I] Every cubic T_i*Phi with Phi a quadric relation lies in the relation ideal, so by Nakayama I^3 is generated mod mI^3+J by the 265 normal monomials. Commands: run d2b.sing-style steps (local `syz` of d=2 as above; build R2 in `ring rT=32009,(T(1..17)),dp;`; `kbase(std(R2),3)`; `map phi=rT,G; ideal Pq=phi(kb);`), then in `ds`: `U=Pq,J,t2*Pq,...,t7*Pq; syz(U)` (1856 gens against 6784) and take h3 = 265 - rank of constants, or `minbase((Pq,J))` with h3 = size-1. Cost: a 3.7x smaller module, still same degree growth; [I] hours on one core. Falsifier: h3 <= 265, rank_C(3) = 969-265 + (new relations) >= 704; reproduces h1=17, h2=85 when the same code runs at d=1,2.
    28	2. **Mod-p linear algebra on the m-adic truncation (no Groebner).** [I] Fix N = order bound (G orders 2-6; cubes <= 18, plus 7-9 for mI^3). Test c in L by solving sum c_b Pr_b = j*J + sum t_k * a_k with a_k in span(Pr) over monomials of degree <= D, via sparse nullspace mod 32009 (FLINT `nmod_mat` or Singular `rank`/`syz` on constant matrices). L only needs cofactors up to the degree where it stabilizes: increase D until rank stabilizes twice. Cost: matrix with C(D+6,6) rows, D~24 gives 593775 rows, feasible by sparse Wiedemann; [I] minutes to hours. Falsifier: same truncation at d=2 returns 68 (h2=85) and rank of d=3 never exceeds 704+ and h3 <= 265, rank monotone in D.
    29	3. **Rees/fiber cone by global degree-wise elimination in T-degree 3 only.** [I] Via Macaulay2 `fiberCone`/`reesAlgebra` on R/J (global dp, prime p) truncated at T-degree 3, then `(Rel + m)` hilbertFunction 3. Same object (special fiber of Rees algebra). [I] The memory note records that full `eliminate` of the Rees graph stalled at 90k pairs, so use only the T-degree <=3 truncation (`degreeLimit`), not full elimination. Falsifier: HF 17, 85 matches; HF3 <= 265.
    30	4. **Parallel mod-p plus CRT / rational lift.** [I] Run option 1 at three or four primes p = 1 mod 4 (32009 with i=10754; 32749 with i=15645) on the 4 vCPU Kaggle box, one prime per core. Gives a coincidence check of h3 across primes; only valid if G over Z[i] reduces consistently. Falsifier: h3 differs between primes.
    31	5. **msolve.** [I] Not a fit: msolve computes zero-dimensional or elimination Groebner bases over a global order and has no syzygy or local-order mode; the repo's measured msolve rows (docs/runbooks/compute-flags.md:164-168) died at memory limits on the larger E8bar->N+ Rees elimination. Use only to cross-check R2 (the Rel_2 ideal) at Hilbert function level, not for h3.
    32	
    33	## 5. Recommendation
