**The highest-value work is a reusable method-A driver plus a completion-certificate layer.** The retained calculations establish useful graded pieces and quadratic models; the remaining bottleneck is proving that those models describe the entire fiber. The decision record explicitly keeps finite Hilbert-function segments separate from the full deliverable. [`decision-record.md:9–14`](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/decision-record.md:9)

Throughout, \(K_2\) means the ideal generated by the certified quadratic relations. Its projective scheme \(V(K_2)\) contains the desired fiber; its dimension and degree become fiber invariants only after a completeness argument.

The old E8-bar→VB run attempted the full object through an expensive presentation. Its ring had twenty variables:
\[
a,\ t_1,\ldots,t_8,\ y_1,\ldots,y_{10},\ h.
\]
The script reduced the ten kernel-coordinate generators modulo \(J\), formed the Rees graph \(J+(y_i-aG_i)\), homogenized it, and called `eliminate(R,a)`. The subsequent, planned stages dehomogenized, specialized \(t=0\), saturated by the target coordinates, and called `minAssGTZ`. [`e8vb_split_homog.sing:2–14`](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/e8vb-old/e8vb_split_homog.sing:2)

The run reached homogenization and remained inside elimination. `RESULT eliminated 0` reports that `elimpart(J)` removed zero variables; it does **not** report successful Rees elimination. The later `PROGRESS rees` marker never appears in the sixteen-line protocol. [`input:4–7`](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/e8vb-old/e8vb_split_homog.sing:4), [`out.log:2–16`](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/e8vb-old/out.log:2)

