**The timeout-extension mechanism did neutralize the original supervisor while the hold remained active.** Line 11 sends `SIGSTOP` to `timeout`; the extension script later resumes that process on exit or at its replacement deadline. A stopped supervisor cannot execute its alarm or ordinary signal handler. If the floor watchdog sent its termination request to that same stopped supervisor, the request could remain pending while Singular continued. The later postmortem records precisely that targeting and says a manual kill ended the run. [`extend-timeout.sh:8–16`](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/e8vb-old/extend-timeout.sh:8), [`decision-record.md:150–156`](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/decision-record.md:150)

That conclusion needs a boundary: the supplied script proves the stop/resume mechanism; the decision record supplies the floor-signal target. `SIGSTOP` would not defeat a direct `SIGKILL` to Singular or an independently enforced cgroup deadline. The retained exit value is 137, which supports forcible termination but alone identifies neither the sender nor its reason. The later postmortem supersedes the earlier statement that the watchdog ended the run. [`exit:1`](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/e8vb-old/exit:1), [`decision-record.md:147–156`](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/decision-record.md:147)

The old run’s failure was therefore an unresolved, single-threaded graph-elimination computation, compounded by ineffective supervision. The growing and replenishing pair frontier explains the poor return; the logs establish neither mathematical nontermination nor an intrinsic memory impossibility. Singular’s individual elimination and standard-basis computations use one thread. [`compute-flags.md:125–132`](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/runbooks/compute-flags.md:125)

The old run retains useful performance and supervision evidence. It retains **no usable fiber ideal, component decomposition, or resumable polynomial checkpoint**: the input writes none before completing elimination. [`e8vb_split_homog.sing:7–14`](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/e8vb-old/e8vb_split_homog.sing:7)

